ent":{"present":true,"statement":"The book argues that society undervalues introverts, having a detrimental cultural impact, and that introverts’ contributions are substantial and should be validated and included.","confidence":0.72},"academicOrientation":{"score":35,"confidence":0.4},"profileConfidence":0.8,"lowerConfidenceCandidates":{"centralFigures":[{"name":"Steve Wozniak","confidence":0.38},{"name":"Rosa Parks","confidence":0.36}]},"model":"gpt-5.4-nano-2026-03-17","promptVersion":8,"inputHash":"09a79abaa248b3fec22e93aa3692e222f030a5b0542cdc5c6a5ce5b6b12f2f73","reviewStatus":"unreviewed","validationWarnings":[]},"primarySubject":"Society & Culture","secondarySubjects":["Gender & Sexuality"],"confidence":"high","rationale":"This book primarily examines the societal perceptions and cultural dynamics surrounding introverts, making 'Society & Culture' the best fit, while also touching on psychological aspects of personality.","method":"llm","model":"gpt-4o-mini","reviewStatus":"generated","inputHash":"1696b780d5c32e55b47493a780277d898bdc3108ab0271e1ae0816e8e207192c","summary":"#1 NEW YORK TIMES BESTSELLER • Experience the book that started the Quiet Movement and revolutionized how the world sees introverts—and how introverts see themselves—by offering validation, inclusion, and inspiration “Superbly researched, deeply insightful, and a fascinating read, Quiet is an indispensable resource for anyone who wants to understand the gifts of the introverted half of the population.”—Gretchen Rubin, author of The Happiness Project ONE OF THE BEST BOOKS OF THE YEAR—People, O: The Oprah Magazine, Christian Science Monitor, Inc., Library Journal, Kirkus Reviews What are the advantages of being an introvert? They make up at least one-third of the people we know. They are the ones who prefer listening to speaking; who innovate and create but dislike self-promotion; who favor working on their own over working in teams. It is to introverts—Rosa Parks, Chopin, Dr. Seuss, Steve Wozniak—that we owe many of the great contributions to society. In Quiet, Susan Cain argues that we dramatically undervalue introverts and shows how much we lose in doing so. She charts the rise of the Extrovert Ideal throughout the twentieth century and explores how deeply it has come to permeate our culture.","pageCount":354,"publicationYear":2012,"subjectCategories":[{"source":"google_books","scheme":"google_books_category","label":"Psychology","sourceId":"source-google-books-summary-quiet-the-power-of-introverts-in-a-world-that-can-t-stop-talking-susan-cain"}],"displaySummary":"In Quiet, Susan Cain argues that we dramatically undervalue introverts and shows how much we lose in doing so. She charts the rise of the Extrovert Ideal throughout the twentieth century and explores how deeply it has come to permeate our culture.","primaryTopic":"Technology, Computing & AI","subjectEvidence":{"primarySubject":"Society & Culture","confidence":"medium","method":"evidence_score","candidates":[{"subject":"Society & Culture","score":8,"evidenceCount":1}],"evidence":[{"source":"llm_classifier","rawLabel":"Society & Culture","mappedSubject":"Society & Culture","score":8,"confidence":"high","note":"This book primarily examines the societal perceptions and cultural dynamics surrounding introverts, making 'Society & Culture' the best fit, while also touching on psychological aspects of personality.","id":"subject-evidence-book-quiet-the-power-of-introverts-in-a-world-that-can-t-stop-talking-susan-cain-1"},{"source":"google_books","scheme":"google_books_category","rawLabel":"Psychology","mappedSubject":"Medicine & Public Health","score":6,"confidence":"high","sourceId":"source-google-books-summary-quiet-the-power-of-introverts-in-a-world-that-can-t-stop-talking-susan-cain","id":"subject-evidence-book-quiet-the-power-of-introverts-in-a-world-that-can-t-stop-talking-susan-cain-3"},{"source":"keyword_classifier","rawLabel":"Religion","mappedSubject":"Religion","score":2,"confidence":"low